WEBVTT

1
00:00:01.000 --> 00:00:04.850
Welcome. You're on a demo site
Salesforce built for Resolvion.

2
00:00:04.910 --> 00:00:08.630
In the next few minutes, you'll see
why we built it, and how to use it.

3
00:00:08.690 --> 00:00:13.570
Every screen follows one assignment,
from lender to close, using sample data.

4
00:00:14.450 --> 00:00:18.630
Every month, more than 50,000
new assignments reach Resolvion.

5
00:00:18.690 --> 00:00:21.280
Over 10,000 vehicles are recovered.

6
00:00:21.340 --> 00:00:25.300
More than 600 contracted recovery
agents work in the field.

7
00:00:25.360 --> 00:00:28.350
And dozens of lenders each
bring their own rules.

8
00:00:29.950 --> 00:00:32.540
Your team has been clear
about where things stand.

9
00:00:32.600 --> 00:00:37.970
A new platform on Azure is going live while
the legacy ERP still runs accounting.

10
00:00:38.030 --> 00:00:43.420
Lender notes arrive in every format, and
your on-site model has to decipher each one.

11
00:00:43.480 --> 00:00:45.283
AI is already working for you,

12
00:00:45.333 --> 00:00:50.390
but the spend is climbing across three
model providers, with no traffic cop.

13
00:00:50.450 --> 00:00:52.870
And borrower data can't leave your hands.

14
00:00:54.470 --> 00:00:57.680
The next connection shouldn't
be another custom project.

15
00:00:57.740 --> 00:01:00.960
Here's how Salesforce would
approach it, in three layers.

16
00:01:02.470 --> 00:01:03.790
First, connect.

17
00:01:03.850 --> 00:01:08.816
MuleSoft builds one governed bridge from
the new platform to the legacy ERP,

18
00:01:08.866 --> 00:01:12.730
accounting first, and reuses
it when the ERP retires.

19
00:01:12.790 --> 00:01:18.700
Every API is MCP-ready, so your production
agents use the same governed connections.

20
00:01:19.500 --> 00:01:20.880
Second, govern.

21
00:01:20.940 --> 00:01:25.860
Agent Fabric sits across the orchestrator,
agents and models you already run.

22
00:01:25.920 --> 00:01:27.520
Nothing is replaced.

23
00:01:27.580 --> 00:01:30.510
It routes each request to
the right model by policy,

24
00:01:30.560 --> 00:01:35.730
keeps borrower data on your on-site model,
and caps spend with Model Wallet budgets.

25
00:01:37.330 --> 00:01:38.410
Third, show.

26
00:01:38.470 --> 00:01:41.884
Tableau gives executives
concise views on governed data,

27
00:01:41.934 --> 00:01:45.450
and puts a live scorecard
inside your agent portal.

28
00:01:45.510 --> 00:01:49.220
On the same foundation, Fin can
take routine borrower calls.

29
00:01:50.330 --> 00:01:52.260
You don't have to do it all at once.

30
00:01:52.320 --> 00:01:55.490
Phase 1 is the bridge your MVP already needs.

31
00:01:55.550 --> 00:01:57.340
Everything else builds on it.

32
00:01:57.400 --> 00:02:00.730
On this site, you'll see each
of these working, step by step.

33
00:02:05.330 --> 00:02:08.520
This site is laid out a little
differently, on purpose.

34
00:02:08.580 --> 00:02:12.700
On the left is what your people see:
the screens they'd use every day.

35
00:02:12.760 --> 00:02:17.256
On the right is the part that's usually
invisible: MuleSoft and Agent Fabric,

36
00:02:17.306 --> 00:02:19.200
doing the work underneath.

37
00:02:19.260 --> 00:02:22.500
Integration and AI governance
can feel abstract.

38
00:02:22.560 --> 00:02:26.449
Putting both sides together shows
you exactly where your data flows,

39
00:02:26.499 --> 00:02:29.290
and what keeps it governed, at every step.

40
00:02:29.350 --> 00:02:31.950
And every stop follows that same assignment.

41
00:02:33.330 --> 00:02:34.550
Choose your route.

42
00:02:34.610 --> 00:02:39.370
The short path covers the key moments:
14 stops in about 15 minutes.

43
00:02:39.430 --> 00:02:45.040
The full run takes about 30 minutes and adds
every stop, with deeper technical detail.

44
00:02:45.690 --> 00:02:48.820
Click whatever's pulsing
to move the story forward.

45
00:02:48.880 --> 00:02:52.400
Here, a lender's hold reaches
the agent's phone in seconds.

46
00:02:52.460 --> 00:02:54.540
When a step is done, press Next.

47
00:02:55.840 --> 00:03:00.300
Here, Agent Fabric routes each request
to the right model, by policy.

48
00:03:02.790 --> 00:03:07.890
And here, each agent sees their own
scorecard, ranked against anonymized peers.

49
00:03:10.090 --> 00:03:13.770
When you're ready, let's map your
bridge and your agent spend together.
